# SRG-APP-000865-WSR-000260  -  CAT II
# The web server must, for password-based authentication, employ automated
# tools to assist the user in selecting strong password authenticators.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000865-WSR-000260
group:           V-264352
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   ORGANIZATIONAL
grade:           D
decidable:       manual
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-004065
control_rev5:    IA-5

contribution:    None that is configurable: the Splunk Web password dialog states and
                 enforces the [splunk_auth] composition rules and rejects a non-compliant
                 password, but that behavior follows from those settings and there is no
                 generator, strength meter, or suggestion feature in web.conf to enable.

external:        An approved password manager or generator for users - carried by the
                 organization's endpoint tooling.
external:        Where authentication is external or fronted by an SSO proxy, the
                 password-selection interface and any assistance it offers belong to that
                 provider.

manual_reason:   No conf key for the web tier enables or configures an automated
                 password-selection aid, so no observed configuration value can decide this
                 requirement.

citation:        splunk-spec-files/authentication.conf.spec:441-500;
                 splunk-spec-files/web.conf.spec:16 ([settings] holds no
                 password-assistance setting)
finding:         Not a finding against the application: Splunk Web has no configurable
                 automated aid for selecting a strong password beyond enforcing the
                 [splunk_auth] composition rules assessed elsewhere, so this requirement is
                 carried by the organization's endpoint tooling and the identity provider;
                 this determination is from the perspective of the application layer alone.
